traduia (0.9.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Allow to use HTTP repository for models set from CLI/env/config
  * Model on disk detection
  * traduia-make-repo helper to generate local repo from downloaded model
  * traduia-open-url wrapper ensure that xdg-open works with valid installed browser
  * Installation from zero-center skipping downloads when already on disk
  * Uninstall from zero-center without remove models
  * Models source selection in zero-center (Internet/USB/LAN) with repo validation
  * Adaptive optimization question from available models
  * lliurex-firefox-settings integration
  * Allow tunable parameters from env
  * Repo validation
  * LliureX Ainur page entry (lliurex-www)
  * traduia-config standalone command
  * Fully offline install from USB/LAN repo (python wheels)
  * traduia-make-repo debs subcommand
  * Client mode installs firefox-settings entry; --disable-meta-checks option
  * zero-center configured state sync; root only for modifying operations
  * Prefer repo deb (USB/LAN debs/) when its version is >= apt's one
  * traduia-make-repo fetch subcommand (direct HuggingFace download, additive)
  * 'all' mode in install-models-traduia and traduia-make-repo (both model sets)
  * Fatal pip errors with install log (/var/log/traduia-install.log)
  * Validate repository wheels before installing them
  * Clean venv rebuild with python3 -m venv --clear
  * Add missing exceptiongroup wheel for Python 3.10
  * Log pip download output on wheels export failures

 -- M.Angel Juan <m.angel.juan@gmail.com>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:06:24 +0200

